<p>You can use the <a href=3D"https://developers.arcgis.com/qt/cpp/api-refe=
rence/esri-arcgisruntime-geometryengine.html"><code>GeometryEngine</code></=
a> to create new geometries from existing geometries by performing operatio=
ns such as these:</p><ul>
<li><strong>Buffer</strong>=E2=80=94Buffer a geometry at a specified distan=
ce, creating a buffer polygon.</li>
<li><strong>Clip</strong>=E2=80=94Create a geometry by clipping a geometry =
with an envelope.</li>
<li><strong>Densify</strong>=E2=80=94Create a densified copy of the input g=
eometry by adding vertices between existing vertices.</li>
<li><strong>Difference</strong>=E2=80=94Create a geometry that is the topol=
ogical difference of two geometries.</li>
<li><strong>Offset</strong>=E2=80=94Create an offset version of the input g=
eometry.</li>
<li><strong>Union</strong>=E2=80=94Create a geometry that is the union of t=
wo or more geometries.</li>
<li><strong>Intersection</strong>=E2=80=94Create a geometry that is the top=
ological intersection of two geometries.</li>
<li><strong>Symmetric</strong> Difference=E2=80=94Create a geometry that is=
 the topological symmetric difference of two geometries.</li>
<li><strong>Simplify</strong>=E2=80=94Makes geometry topologically consiste=
nt according to the geometry type. For instance, it rectifies polygons that=
 may be self-intersecting, or contain incorrect ring orientations.</li>
</ul>
